{
  "_comment": "How much a pre-portioned seasoning container holds, in grams, plus the teaspoon range a cook should measure. HelloFresh publishes no weight for these, so before this file the mass was a flat 8 g per sachet and the teaspoon figure lived in a separate table that drifted out of step with it — the UI once said 'half a tsp of ground cloves' while the planner bought 8 g, an implied 16 g/tsp against a real 2.1. Here `grams` is the single canonical number and teaspoons are always derived from it as grams / g_per_tsp, so the two can no longer disagree. `g_per_tsp` is a published density constant, not a guess; the only estimated quantity is the container mass itself. `source` records which masses are real: 'measured' entries were read off delivered packaging and must never be overwritten by an automated pass. tsp_min/tsp_max bound what a sensible cook would use in a base-yield (2 serving) dish; they drive the displayed range and act as a guardrail on the mass. Resolution: exact by_name -> defaults by unit and kind. See app/canonicalize.py (spice_dose) and app/measures.py.",
  "defaults": {
    "sachet(s)": {
      "dry": {
        "grams": 4.5,
        "g_per_tsp": 2.3,
        "tsp_min": 1.0,
        "tsp_max": 3.0,
        "note": "Rebased from a flat 8 g onto the two measured sachets (3.5 g and 5 g). Both are spice mixes — the dominant seasoning of their dish — so they sit at the top of the range and an unlisted dry sachet should sit a little under them."
      },
      "wet": {
        "grams": 15.0,
        "g_per_tsp": 5.5,
        "tsp_min": 1.0,
        "tsp_max": 4.0,
        "note": "Purees, pastes and condiments in sachet form. Denser and larger than a spice dose; a mayonnaise or ginger puree sachet is a tablespoon-ish, not a teaspoon."
      }
    },
    "pot(s)": {
      "dry": {
        "grams": 7.0,
        "g_per_tsp": 2.3,
        "tsp_min": 1.5,
        "tsp_max": 5.0,
        "note": "Pots hold more than sachets. Scaled from the sachet default by the ratio the old flat constants assumed (12/8), applied to the corrected sachet mass."
      },
      "wet": {
        "grams": 30.0,
        "g_per_tsp": 5.5,
        "tsp_min": 2.0,
        "tsp_max": 8.0,
        "note": "Peanut butter, mustards, curry pastes."
      }
    }
  },
